As we iterate through each diagonal, we start by initializing the row index (j) to the diagonal index (d - n + 1) and the column index (i) to the diagonal index (d). We continue adding elements to the order array until we reach the end of the diagonal, which is when the row index is greater than or equal to the column index.

Note that we use Math.min(d, n - 1) to ensure that we never access an element beyond the boundaries of the matrix for the second dimension.

